OL,3,GNEWSAParents' safety plea as lollipop
OL,4,Aworkers face axe
OL,5,
OL,6,FParents in Worcestershire have hit out
OL,7,Fover the potential scrapping of
OL,8,Flollipop patrols, with one calling it
OL,9,F"senseless".
OL,11,FWorcestershire County Council is
OL,12,Fconsidering axing its school crossing
OL,13,Fpatrol service, putting up to 18 jobs
OL,14,Fat risk.
OL,16,FKatherine Forster, a parent at Cherry
OL,17,FOrchard Primary School in Worcester,
OL,18,Fsaid: "It's a really bad idea to take
OL,19,Ffunding away from child safety."
OL,23,APub: 26-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,357,350,200,160,0,100
